Question 7: Given arr = np.arange(1, 13).reshape(2, 2, 3), print 6, then the first row of the second block ([7 8 9]), then the last element using negative indices (12).

AIM: Printing specified elements and slices of array

Code:
import numpy as np
arr=np.arange(1, 13).reshape(2, 2, 3)
print(arr[0][1][2])
print("First row of second block:\t",arr[1][0])
print("Last element:",arr[1][1][2])

Output:
 6
First row of second block:       [7 8 9]
Last element:    12

Explanation:
Key Concept: Array Slicing- usage of chain indexing.
Note: Instead of chain indexing, it can also be written as arr[0,1,2].
